CM_ "ARS510 radar bus (comma harness bus 1), frame-local view. The 0x80 object list and 0x85 metadata record are segmented over many frames and are reassembled in code (ars510.transport); their frames appear here only as raw bytes. Decoded objects are in ars510_objects_vbus.dbc. Documentation: github.com/ds-sebastian/ars510-radar docs/.";
CM_ BO_ 128 "0x80 object-list transport: a 742-byte record (20 object slots + CRC32) sent every 60 ms as 106 ISO-TP-like frames. First frame starts 12 E4; bytes 1-7 of each frame are appended.";
CM_ BO_ 133 "0x85 metadata-record transport: a 147-byte record (prefix, ten 12-byte cells, CRC32) sent every 60 ms as 21 frames. First frame starts 10 90.";
CM_ BO_ 129 "Record-cycle marker: 30 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 within 20 ms after each 0x80 record start.";
CM_ BO_ 134 "Record-cycle marker: 30 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 within 20 ms after each 0x85 record start.";
CM_ BO_ 256 "Startup context: word 0 is 0xFFFF in the first frame after power-up, zero afterwards.";
CM_ BO_ 257 "Radar startup state: 0x1D while booting, 0x11 once running (switches 70 ms before 0x197 bit 8 sets).";
CM_ BO_ 258 "Sparse state bits 11, 14 and 21.";
CM_ BO_ 259 "Always zero.";
CM_ BO_ 384 "Constant CF C0 00 00 00.";
CM_ BO_ 400 "Radar cycle header (16.7 Hz): microsecond timestamp and a mod-16 cycle counter.";
CM_ BO_ 401 "Selected-target companion A (with 0x192): score, age and track code of a target the radar selects itself. Sentinel FE FE FE FC FC FF FE FF = no target.";
CM_ BO_ 402 "Selected-target summary A (4 bytes): distance and lateral position of one target of the radar's internal tracker, in the object list's encoding. Sentinel 00 FF 00 FF = no target.";
CM_ BO_ 403 "Selected-target companion B (with 0x194); same layout as 0x191.";
CM_ BO_ 404 "Selected-target summary B; same layout as 0x192.";
CM_ BO_ 405 "Event frame, paired with 0x196: idle 99.97% of the time, active during rare events.";
CM_ BO_ 406 "Event frame, paired with 0x195.";
CM_ BO_ 407 "Startup phase: bit 8 sets once the radar is running and stays set.";
CM_ BO_ 408 "Constant 0x10.";
CM_ BO_ 514 "Counter frame: byte 1 high nibble counts mod 16; byte 0 is a check byte that depends only on the counter.";
CM_ BO_ 528 "Copy of Toyota road-sign-assist data (speed-sign presence, speed-limit value, TSR switch).";
CM_ BO_ 565 "The radar's ACC target, 50 Hz (content per 60 ms radar cycle): closing speed, relative acceleration, lateral speed and acceleration and the target ID. Position and in-path state are on 0x237.";
CM_ SG_ 565 A235_ACC_TARGET_VREL "Closing speed of the ACC target, m/s, negative = closing; 0.125 m/s per code (stopped leads, distance slope).";
CM_ SG_ 565 A235_ACC_TARGET_AREL "Relative acceleration of the ACC target (positive = opening): (code - 100) * 0.125 m/s^2; one code is one speed code per second (closure 1.00 over 2 s windows). Code 100 is the idle value.";
CM_ SG_ 565 A235_ACC_TARGET_VLAT "Lateral speed of the ACC target, left positive, about 0.0125 m/s per code (the lateral position changes by 1.2 cm per code-second).";
CM_ SG_ 565 A235_ACC_TARGET_ALAT "Relative lateral acceleration of the ACC target, left positive: (code - 100) * 0.125 m/s^2 (nominal unit, as the longitudinal field). Mostly minus the ego lateral acceleration (-8.2 codes per m/s^2), plus a lateral-speed term; lags the yaw rate by about 0.5 s.";
CM_ SG_ 565 A235_TARGET_ID5 "Target identity: constant while the radar follows one target; 31 with the idle payload.";
CM_ BO_ 567 "The OEM ACC target witness, 50 Hz: lateral position and distance of the target the stock ACC follows (see 0x235).";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_ACC_TARGET_LAT "Lateral position of the ACC target, m, left positive: 12 bits, (code - 2000) * 0.01. One object-list lateral code is exactly 1.5 of these codes.";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_TRACKER_A8 "Raw tracker byte: 35-36 on a steady target, 44-50 while it accelerates, 48-93 while it brakes.";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_TRACKER_B8 "Raw tracker byte: about 88 for a stopped target, 97-139 for a steady mover, rises toward 240 (and wraps) while the target accelerates or brakes.";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_TARGET_PRESENT "1 with an ACC target.";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_IN_PATH_CONFIRMED "1 while the target is confirmed in the path (level 5).";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_IN_PATH_CANDIDATE "1 while the target is a candidate (levels 4-2).";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_IN_PATH_LEVEL3 "In-path level 5, 4, 3, 2; steps to the neighbouring level only; lower levels sit farther from the path.";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_ACC_TARGET_DIST_COARSE "Nominal distance of the ACC target in about 5.26 m steps (+9.6 m), an empirical reference-dependent conversion; the top 5 bits of A237_ACC_TARGET_DISTANCE_CODE.";
CM_ SG_ 567 A237_ACC_TARGET_DISTANCE_CODE "Distance of the ACC target, 0.025 m per code, zero offset (0.02 m median residual against the 0x680 object range).";
CM_ BO_ 569 "50 Hz companion of the ACC target: target class, object-list flag and the radar cycle timestamp of the 0x235 / 0x237 content.";
CM_ BO_ 571 "50 Hz companion of the ACC target (3 bytes): CRC-8, counter and the target width in cm.";
CM_ BO_ 573 "Always zero.";
CM_ BO_ 576 "Context frame, 16.7 Hz, rolling phase 1-7 in byte 0. Carries changing payloads (paired with 0x244) on some drives; default body otherwise.";
CM_ BO_ 577 "Context frame, 16.7 Hz, rolling phase 1-7 in byte 0; default body.";
CM_ BO_ 580 "Context frame, 16.7 Hz, rolling phase 1-7 in byte 0. Carries changing payloads (paired with 0x240) on some drives; bytes 4 and 7 are always equal.";
CM_ BO_ 581 "Context frame, 16.7 Hz, rolling phase 1-7 in byte 0; default body.";
CM_ BO_ 584 "Startup / event context frame with the same rolling phase as 0x240-0x245.";
CM_ BO_ 589 "State frame: 00 00 00 00 00 00 56 normally; 00 00 00 00 02 00 58 in a rare second state.";
CM_ BO_ 591 "Startup phase: bit 6 sets once the radar is running.";
CM_ BO_ 1280 "Constant, unit-specific payload (redacted here; compare your own).";
CM_ BO_ 1281 "Slow status frame: constants plus a 4-bit state at bit 40.";
CM_ BO_ 1282 "Slow state frame (every 3 s): two slowly drifting codes (bytes 1 and 2-3) and a unit-specific constant tail (redacted).";
CM_ BO_ 1664 "One object from the radar's function-level tracker (2 Hz): mostly a stationary roadside object, sometimes a vehicle. Idle payload 00 00 08 00 80 00 80 0A.";
CM_ SG_ 514 A202_CHECK_BYTE8 "Check byte, a fixed function of A202_COUNTER4: 0:10 1:8D 2:37 3:AA 4:5E 5:C3 6:79 7:E4 8:8C 9:11 10:AB 11:36 12:C2 13:5F 14:E5 15:78 (hex).";
